{"version":1,"ops":[{"type":1,"author":{"id":"607ac2a9afabc0e44debe80e34283e413e009770"},"timestamp":1528340604,"metadata":{"github-id":"MDU6SXNzdWUzMzAxMDAxOTk=","github-url":"https://github.com/datalad/datalad/issues/2628","origin":"github"},"title":"config: Parser respresents multiple entries as tuples, which callers don't handle","message":"If a value occurs multiple times in the git configuration, it's represented as a tuple.\n\nhttps://github.com/datalad/datalad/blob/1bdc37a5ec2e8d63bba541e7c9c0778b4559fd89/datalad/config.py#L79-L85\n\nAFAICS most, if not all, callers of `config.get` and friends do not handle this multi-value case. This means that I can't set a value in `.gitconfig` and then override it in the repo's `.git/config` (e.g., if I want to enable `datalad.run.record-sidecar` in general, but disable it in a specific repo).\n\n---\n\n```bash\n#!/bin/sh\nset -e\n\nmkdir -p /tmp/dl/\nexport HOME=/tmp/dl/\n\ngit config --global user.name \"blah\"\ngit config --global user.email \"blah@blah\"\n\nrepo=/tmp/dl/config-test\n\ntest -e $repo \u0026\u0026 datalad remove --nocheck $repo\n\ndatalad create $repo\n\ncd $repo\ngit config --global datalad.run.record-sidecar true\ngit config datalad.run.record-sidecar false\n\npycmd=$(tr \"\\n\" \" \" \u003c\u003c-EOF\n        from datalad.api import Dataset;\n        d = Dataset('.');\n        print(d.config.get('datalad.run.record-sidecar'));\n        print(d.config.getbool('datalad', 'run.record-sidecar'))\nEOF\n)\n\npython -c \"$pycmd\"\n```\n\n```\nremove(ok): /tmp/dl/config-test (dataset)\n[INFO   ] Creating a new annex repo at /tmp/dl/config-test\ncreate(ok): /tmp/dl/config-test (dataset)\n('true', 'false')\nTraceback (most recent call last):\n  File \"\u003cstring\u003e\", line 1, in \u003cmodule\u003e\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/config.py\", line 473, in getbool\n    return anything2bool(val)\n  File \"/home/kyle/src/python/datalad/datalad/config.py\", line 113, in anything2bool\n    % repr(val))\nTypeError: Got value ('true', 'false') which could not be interpreted as a boolean\n```","files":null}]}